## keygraphjs Changelog


### Current WIP

New feature: support for **directed graphs** (in addition to undirected ones).

- global **directed/undirected mode** with a toolbar toggle (`Mode: …`); the mode
  is stored in the JSON (`"directed": true`) and shown in the stats line
- destructive actions ask for confirmation: switching the graph mode, and
  **"New complete graph"** (which replaces the current graph)
- conversion rules: undirected → directed doubles the edge count (each edge
  becomes two directed edges, weights copied); directed → undirected merges a
  bidirectional pair into one edge using the **mean** weight (a lone directed
  edge is kept as-is)
- directed edges are drawn with **arrow tips**; a bidirectional pair (A→B and B→A)
  renders as a **single line with an arrowhead at both ends** (no second curve)
- per-direction edge **weights**; on the canvas a pair's label shows both numbers
  ("0.90 | 0.30"; first = lower-id → higher-id), the tooltip lists both directions
- "Add node → fully connected" adds edges in **both directions** in directed mode;
  "Connect nodes" treats A→B and B→A as distinct edges; right-clicking a collapsed
  pair deletes **both** directions (use the list to delete a single direction)
- import/export: GML `directed 1/0`, GraphML `edgedefault=`, DOT `digraph` / `->`;
  mixed graphs (per-edge overrides of the graph default) are rejected on import

### v0.1.0 -- Initial release

Most relevant features:

- display and edit undirected graphs, option for edge weights and vertex weights
- drag nodes and run a one-shot force-directed **auto-layout** (with undo)
- add and remove nodes, and connect nodes to add edges
- edit edge **weights** (0–1) per edge, or select several and set them all at once
- set a **node weight** (0–1) per node — heavier nodes draw larger and export with the weight
- give nodes human-readable **names** and arbitrary **groups** (colors are assigned automatically)
- toggle edge-weight labels in the view
- **load and save** graphs in JSON or standard formats (GML, GraphML)
